7. Testing and regression prevention

ALVA is a framework-free HTML, CSS, and JavaScript game using ES modules and Canvas 2D.

The repository already has Node.js tests.

Run:

node --test

Add regression tests

Add or update tests that cover:

Capitalization

* Ordinary English interface labels use sentence case.
* French capitalization remains valid.
* Uppercase CSS transformations cannot reintroduce the issue.
* ALVA, CPU, P1, and combat-announcement exceptions are preserved.
* Dynamic translated labels also use the correct capitalization.

Hover and focus

* Opening a screen does not create an unintended hover appearance.
* Programmatic focus does not imitate mouse hover.
* Pointer entry enables hover.
* Pointer exit disables hover.
* Keyboard and controller navigation remain visible and usable.
* Touch interaction cannot produce sticky hover states.
* Persistent selection is separate from hover.

Glass styling

* Every relevant dialogue uses the shared glass treatment.
* Dialogue-specific styles do not replace it with an opaque surface.
* Backdrop-filter fallback behavior remains supported.
* Text remains readable.

Button geometry

* All rectangular menu buttons use the shared 3px corner radius.
* Deliberately circular controls retain their geometry.

Dialogue stacking

* A newly opened dialogue is always topmost.
* Only the topmost dialogue is interactive.
* Parent dialogues become interactive again when children close.
* Escape, gamepad Back, and focus restoration work correctly.
* Closing an entire dialogue chain restores the normal screen.
* No stale z-index, inert, or navigation scope remains.

